          "name": "Choice Scarf",
          "pokemon": "Krokorok",
          "shiny": false,
          "gender": "DC",
          "levels": [],
          "description": "<p>Choice Scarf Krokorok is a solid form of speed control that can also act as a late-game sweeper. With Moxie, Krokorok constantly threatens to run away with the game, only fearing being revenge killed by faster Choice Scarf users such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/monferno/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Monferno</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/girafarig/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Girafarig</a>, as well as strong priority moves from <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/piloswine/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Piloswine</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/thwackey/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Thwackey</a>. Earthquake makes for an excellent late-game sweeping tool once Ground-immunitie and -resistant foes have been dealt with. Knock Off guarantees progress in the mid-game. Stone Edge allows Krokorok to OHKO <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/fletchinder/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Fletchinder</a>, which is often the only Ground-immune Pokemon standing between it and an Earthquake sweep. Brick Break hits <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/scraggy/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Scraggy</a>, Piloswine, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/dunsparce/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Dunsparce</a> harder than Earthquake under Grassy Terrain while also breaking dual screens. Aqua Tail is an option to deal more damage to Piloswine and opposing Krokorok. Stealth Rock is a niche option on teams desperate for a Stealth Rock setter. It can also potentially bluff a non-Choice Scarf set.</p>\n<p>Choice Scarf Krokorok fits on teams that need both strong speed control and a solid cleaner. For instance, defensively oriented entry hazard stacking structures appreciate Krokorok's Knock Off and late-game offensive pressure. Offensively, Krokorok appreciates hazard support from the likes of <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/quilladin/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Quilladin</a>, Dunsparce, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/glimmet/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Glimmet</a> to secure OHKOs against the likes of defensive <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/drakloak/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Drakloak</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/tinkatuff/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Tinkatuff</a>. Krokorok also needs help breaking Water- and Grass-type physical walls such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/quaxwell/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Quaxwell</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/ivysaur/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Ivysaur</a>, and Quilladin. Strong special attackers such as Drakloak, Girafarig, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/sliggoo-hisui/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Sliggoo</a>, as well as Fire-types such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/raboot/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Raboot</a>, Monferno, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/pignite/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Pignite</a>, help here. Defensively, Krokorok needs sturdy answers to Pokemon that can revenge kill it, such as Quaxwell for Choice Scarf Monferno and Piloswine, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/koffing/nfe/\" hreflang=\"en\">Koffing</a> for Thwackey, and Hisuian Sliggoo for Choice Scarf Girafarig. Fletchinder is an exceptional teammate for Krokorok, countering major threats to Krokorok such as Monferno and Thwackey on account of its great defensive typing, STAB Brave Bird, and, for the latter, Flame Body. Ivysaur is another strong partner for Krokorok since its typing enables it to deal with Water- and Grass-types both offensively and defensively. It also absorbs Toxic Spikes, which Krokorok appreciates, while Ivysaur appreciates Krokorok's Psychic-type immunity.</p>",
